{"entryId":"3200","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3200:1","sourceSha256":"16f35a6650ee2cfd363c0f55367035e87d1d034db954595f69b9c665ac4b48a9","englishSha256":"2a127decbf8b8efabffaab19622977f40a0b830827e5e10940ccbba38d5382cb","citations":[{"id":"3200:1:link-001","he":[12,45],"en":[16,63],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_32a.11"},"reference":"Gittin 32a:11","assessment":"Gittin gives Rabbah bar Aivu in Rav Sheshet’s name, or alternatively Rabbah bar Avuha.","evidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 32a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_32a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3200:1:link-002","he":[46,55],"en":[65,83],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Gittin_32a.11.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Gittin 32a:11:1","assessment":"Tosafot explicitly reject making Rav Sheshet the authority in the alternate Rabbah bar Avuha version.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Gittin 32a:11:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Gittin_32a.11.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3200:1:link-003","he":[57,82],"en":[84,109],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_23a.8"},"reference":"Ketubot 23a:8","assessment":"The separate Ketubot passage gives Rabbah bar Avin. Similarity of the names alone does not establish one person.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 23a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_23a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[{"raw":"אולי אחד הוא","reason":"Gittin and Ketubot independently attest the Aivu and Avin spellings. Neither source establishes a personal identification.","evidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 32a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_32a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 23a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_23a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Gittin and Tosafot give the Aivu transmission and distinguish the alternate Avuha. Ketubot gives Avin. The proposed identification remains open.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
